WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.504 --> 00:00:12.865
stomped her boots on the floor.

2
00:00:14.265 --> 00:00:16.186
Her mom had forgotten to pack her sneakers.

3
00:00:16.847 --> 00:00:19.128
So she had to wear these hot boots all day.

4
00:00:19.988 --> 00:00:23.449
Nina's baby sister, Lulu, took up most of Mom's time now.

5
00:00:23.469 --> 00:00:26.971
"Baby first," her mom always said.

6
00:00:26.991 --> 00:00:32.270
"Nina, please join us for the craft," Miss Shelly said.

7
00:00:33.892 --> 00:00:35.253
Nina slowly walked over.

8
00:00:37.795 --> 00:00:40.277
The table was covered in orange, brown, and green.

9
00:00:40.297 --> 00:00:43.820
"It looks like a pumpkin patch!"

10
00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:44.801
Izzie said.

11
00:00:44.821 --> 00:00:49.665
"We're going to make yarn pumpkins," Miss Shelly said.

12
00:00:49.685 --> 00:00:52.067
"Everyone will work with a partner.

13
00:00:52.747 --> 00:00:56.890
The pumpkins have to dry overnight, so it will take two days.

14
00:00:58.111 --> 00:00:59.908
Bobby, I'll work with you."

15
00:01:01.309 --> 00:01:02.889
Izzie and Jason were partners.

16
00:01:04.009 --> 00:01:05.010
Ethan looked at Nina.

17
00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:06.590
"Want to be partners?"

18
00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:08.311
Nina blushed.

19
00:01:08.951 --> 00:01:12.032
"Okay." She looked at the instructions.

20
00:01:12.052 --> 00:01:16.293
"First, blow up a balloon about halfway.

21
00:01:16.953 --> 00:01:18.893
This will be the size of your pumpkin."

22
00:01:19.754 --> 00:01:21.574
Nina blew up her balloon halfway.

23
00:01:21.594 --> 00:01:28.136
"Tie a piece of yarn to the balloon and hang it from a stick," Ethan said.

24
00:01:29.116 --> 00:01:31.518
Nina tied the string while Ethan held the stick.

25
00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:39.606
"Great. Now dunk one string of yarn into your glue bowl," Miss Shelly said.

26
00:01:39.626 --> 00:01:43.429
"You can use a plastic fork to help with the dipping."

27
00:01:44.690 --> 00:01:47.232
Nina gently slid the yarn through the plastic fork.

28
00:01:48.213 --> 00:01:50.335
She giggled as she dipped.

29
00:01:50.355 --> 00:01:52.617
"This part is fun!"

30
00:01:52.637 --> 00:01:55.400
"One partner holds the stick.

31
00:01:56.424 --> 00:01:58.925
The other wraps the yarn around the balloon.

32
00:02:00.445 --> 00:02:03.766
Carefully press the yarns' ends down on the balloon.

33
00:02:04.947 --> 00:02:07.187
They must stick," Miss Shelly said.

34
00:02:08.148 --> 00:02:10.128
Nina dipped more yarn into glue.

35
00:02:10.148 --> 00:02:13.489
"Now we repeat the steps one more time," Ethan said.

36
00:02:13.509 --> 00:02:17.650
"You can make a few more pumpkins," Miss Shelly said.

37
00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:20.311
"The pumpkins must dry overnight.

38
00:02:21.131 --> 00:02:22.952
So we'll finish them tomorrow."

39
00:02:24.084 --> 00:02:27.225
"I want to make four pumpkins," Nina said.

40
00:02:28.905 --> 00:02:30.686
She blew up two larger balloons.

41
00:02:32.126 --> 00:02:34.247
Then she blew up one very small balloon.

42
00:02:38.948 --> 00:02:41.369
Finally everyone set their sticks on the table.

43
00:02:42.589 --> 00:02:43.909
The pumpkins had to dry.

44
00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:49.731
The next day Izzie pointed to Nina's dried balloons.

45
00:02:49.751 --> 00:02:52.052
"A baby pumpkin!

46
00:02:52.392 --> 00:02:55.177
Cute!" "Is that baby Lulu?"

47
00:02:55.497 --> 00:02:56.378
Jason asked.

48
00:02:57.139 --> 00:02:58.300
Nina was surprised.

49
00:02:58.320 --> 00:02:59.981
"You can tell?"

50
00:03:00.001 --> 00:03:04.145
"No, I mean, is that baby Lulu?"

51
00:03:04.685 --> 00:03:06.407
Jason pointed to the gym door.

52
00:03:11.712 --> 00:03:12.612
Nina jumped up.

53
00:03:12.632 --> 00:03:17.957
"Shh, she fell asleep," Nina's mom whispered.

54
00:03:17.977 --> 00:03:21.020
"So I decided to pick you up early."

55
00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:24.482
"Does that mean you can help me with my craft?"

56
00:03:24.883 --> 00:03:26.104
Nina asked hopefully.

57
00:03:26.124 --> 00:03:32.189
"Yes!" Nina showed her the four pumpkins.

58
00:03:33.110 --> 00:03:37.273
"What a beautiful family of pumpkins," Nina's mom said.

59
00:03:37.293 --> 00:03:40.656
"It's our family," Nina said.

60
00:03:41.497 --> 00:03:45.540
Miss Shelly showed everyone how to push on the dry balloons to release them from the yarn.

61
00:03:46.641 --> 00:03:49.444
Next they cut a hole at the top to let out the air.

62
00:03:50.388 --> 00:03:51.769
Then they pulled out the balloons.

63
00:03:55.790 --> 00:03:58.912
make vines and a stem," Miss Shelly said.

64
00:03:59.912 --> 00:04:03.153
Izzie wrapped a green pipe cleaner around each pointer finger.

65
00:04:03.173 --> 00:04:05.694
"Curly vines!"

66
00:04:06.795 --> 00:04:09.036
Nina and her mom picked up their pipe cleaners.

67
00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:12.717
Just then baby Lulu let out a cry.

68
00:04:13.798 --> 00:04:15.118
Nina's mom rushed over.

69
00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:18.640
Nina smiled.

70
00:04:19.561 --> 00:04:21.989
"I guess I'll finish my pumpkins at home.

71
00:04:22.772 --> 00:04:23.675
Baby first!"
